 "notes": [
  "topology: source -> pool -> {sweep declares the window; one recorder at reach 1}. One form throughout, the full luma plane at source sampling; the crop (2144, 982, 1024, 1024) is derived inside the recorder's own envelope. 01-reentry's topology exactly.",
  "core shape: 1 fetch thread, 2 recorder threads, every node PARALLEL, request depth 1. The drawn arm adds one display thread at 16.7 ms; the landed arm adds none.",
  "load stands in for a slower machine: 4 threads doing 512x512 float32 matmuls, which release the GIL and contend for cores rather than for the interpreter. Read paint_summary first \u2014 if load did not move it, the loaded arm is not a slower machine and nothing below is a result.",
  "window: rows 3768..3928 (160 frames) at 23.976 fps, of 11304 listed. Nothing else declares, so the fill is one sequential run and the fetch thread never preempts.",
  "compute_ms is not comparable ACROSS arms: StepNode holds its derived crops between rows (binding.Held) and the renderer re-derives both every paint, because a display draws the row it is on. Within an arm across loads it is the same code, which is the only comparison made of it here.",
  "The comparison is each arm against ITSELF under two loads. Comparing landed against drawn is not the measurement: their sets differ by construction, since one records every row and the other records whatever the frontier was when it painted.",
  "3 repeats, arms interleaved within each repeat, for the reason 01-reentry recorded: every arm is slower in the last repeat than in the first, by more than the arms differ.",
  "landed: quiet and loaded recorded identical sets in 3/3 repeats. Rows only the quiet run recorded, per repeat: [0, 0, 0]; only the loaded run: [0, 0, 0]. Values disagreeing on shared rows: [0, 0, 0].",
  "drawn: quiet and loaded recorded identical sets in 0/3 repeats. Rows only the quiet run recorded, per repeat: [25, 26, 31]; only the loaded run: [43, 53, 44]. Values disagreeing on shared rows: [0, 0, 0]."
